---
description: Read or copy real data only; never modify sources or attack them
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the user data restriction in the repository-root AGENTS.md in every task.
Real production/shared/persistent development data may be read or copied using
read-only credentials. Never write, delete, migrate, change indexes/configuration,
or attack a real source; disable automatic startup writes during source access.
Security tests must create their own temporary MongoDB with synthetic data or a
sanitized copy, skip real .env loading, and assert the generated test URI differs
from the source before connecting. Keep exports private and out of Git/logs.
Do not use real provider services without separate authorization and dedicated
test accounts with synthetic inputs. Never notify real users or validate found secrets.
Never stop an existing database to simulate an outage; stop only the owned fixture.
